# OboxSTEAM Mobile — Project Context

> Load when working on features, auth, routing, or API wiring. Engineering: `expo-engineering-rule.mdc`. UI: `styling-rule.mdc`. Endpoints: `src/lib/api/**` + `api-spec.mdc`. Agent entry: `AGENTS.md`.

---

## What this repo is

**OboxSTEAM.Mobile** — Expo (React Native) app sharing the same backend as `OboxSTEAM.FE` (`EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL`). Web FE stays on VPS; this app is Android-first (Expo Go / EAS APK).

**In scope:** Parent tabs (children / progress, notifications, profile; Schedule when shipped). Thin Student (schedule + check-in) and Mentor (QR + capture) surfaces that reuse the same tokens/components.

**Out of scope:** Manager / Expert / LMS chrome, inventing new backend endpoints, shared npm packages with FE, copying FE `components/ui`.

---

## Actors (mobile)

| Actor | Mobile treatment |
|-------|------------------|
| **Parent** | Primary role — children home, progression, notifications, profile |
| **Student** | Thin — schedule + check-in (when APIs ready) |
| **Mentor** | Thin — session QR + media capture (when APIs ready) |
| Other roles | “Dùng website” + logout — `blocked` pattern |

**Parent–Child linking:** Parent sees linked children via `GET /api/parent/links`. Link/approve/magic-login/complete-profile flows mirror FE Parent dialogs as RN screens when exposed.

---

## Product domain (short)

OboxSTEAM is a Vietnamese STEAM learning platform. Parents register/link children and monitor progress/notifications. Portfolio and manager tools stay on the **web FE**. Mobile adds Parent progress UX plus lightweight Student/Mentor check-in/capture.

---

## Routing (Expo Router)

```text
app/
├── (auth)/
│   └── login.tsx
├── (guest)/
│   └── welcome.tsx
├── (app)/                        → tabs after auth (Parent today)
│   ├── _layout.tsx
│   ├── children/
│   │   ├── index.tsx             → children list
│   │   └── [studentId]/
│   │       ├── index.tsx         → child progression
│   │       └── enrollments/[enrollmentId].tsx
│   ├── notifications.tsx
│   └── profile.tsx
├── blocked.tsx                   → non-supported role
└── _layout.tsx
```

v2: role-based root after `me` — Parent → children home; Student → schedule/check-in; Mentor → session tools; others → `blocked`. Parent tabs add **Lịch** when Schedule ships.

Deep links (as needed): magic-login, approve-link, parent checkout → `expo-linking` / `Linking.openURL(checkoutUrl)`.

